# Pilot artifact contract v1

Each track writes `dossiers.json`, `REPORT.md`, `sources-ledger.json`, and local `sources/` artifacts. Output paths below are relative to the track directory; no absolute paths or traversal outside it. Source artifacts are actual retrieved content, not reconstructed text. All full source bodies are local research copies; public redistribution rights are not inferred.

## dossiers.json

Top-level object:

- `schema_version`: integer 1
- `track`: `newman`, `eucharist`, or `religious-freedom`
- `sources`: source record array, unique `source_id` within this track
- `dossiers`: exactly four dossier records with the frozen IDs for this track
- `acquisition_gaps`: array of factual strings, empty only if none

Required source record fields:

- `source_id`: nonblank ASCII identifier (letters/digits/_/./:/-)
- `title`, `document_kind`, `language`, `source_version`, `work_date`, `witness_edition`, `edition_status`, `translator`, `publisher_or_host`: nonempty strings; use explicit `unknown`/`not_applicable` where appropriate, not a fabricated value
- `url`: actual final public source URL
- `retrieved_at_utc`: observed retrieval timestamp
- `rights_status`: nonempty string, including whether redistribution is unresolved
- `raw_path`, `raw_sha256`, `text_path`, `text_sha256`: paths relative to track root, lowercase 64-hex SHA256 of actual raw and extracted UTF-8 file bytes
- `extraction_notes`: nonempty string; retain actual extraction method and extraction/edition limitations
- `provenance_limitations`: string array

Preserve larger/raw PDF witnesses if required; the selected UTF-8 text source supplied to Synoptics must fit its 2,000,000-byte bound. If splitting is necessary, record a derived passage witness and its relation to the full raw snapshot explicitly, retaining locators; do not silently truncate.

Required dossier record fields:

- `case_id`: N1–N4, E1–E4, or R1–R4 as appropriate
- `title`, `question`: nonempty strings
- `passages`: nonempty passage array (at least two for substantive comparisons; failed counterpart acquisition remains a documented gap)
- `propositions`: nonempty array of objects with `statement` (nonempty text), `evidence_passage_ids` (nonempty list resolving within this dossier), and `qualifications` (array)
- `inference_chain`: nonempty array of strings. For Newman distinguish original premises, witness, inference, conclusion, and our objection; otherwise record comparison reasoning.
- `continuity_reading`: object with `statement`, `evidence_passage_ids`, `assumptions` (array), `strongest_objection`
- `rupture_reading`: same shape; for Newman this is the strongest counterargument to the reconstructed argument, not a fabricated historical rupture claim
- `newman_profile`: object with exactly the seven keys below; each value has `status` (supported_candidate, challenged, undetermined, or not_applicable), `evidence_passage_ids` (array), `rationale` (nonempty string)
- `provisional_assessment`: object with `label` (reconstruction_only, reaffirmation_candidate, development_candidate, scope_difference_candidate, unresolved_tension, contradiction_candidate, or insufficient_evidence) and `rationale` (nonempty string)
- `human_review_status`: exactly `pending`
- `gaps`, `next_evidence`: arrays of strings

Seven note keys:
`preservation_of_type`, `continuity_of_principles`, `power_of_assimilation`, `logical_sequence`, `anticipation_of_future`, `conservative_action`, `chronic_vigour`.

Passage object:

- `passage_id`: unique ASCII identifier within this dossier, preferably prefixed with case ID
- `source_id`: resolves to source record
- `locator`: nonempty historical/printed paragraph/section/page locator. Extracted line alone is not a historical locator.
- `quote`: exact nonempty substring of the stored decoded text, including actual whitespace/newlines; select by slicing source text, not manual retyping
- `start`, `end`: integer half-open Unicode-codepoint offsets, not booleans
- `context_before`, `context_after`: up to 300 codepoints immediately surrounding the quote, sliced from the same decoded text
- `context_note`: interpretive context/attribution note, not a fabricated quotation
- `normative_context`: object documenting speaker/issuer, audience, subject, modality, scope, conditions; use explicit uncertainty where evidence is incomplete

## Scholarly reports

REPORT.md explains the actual case findings and gaps with track-local ledger citations generated by grounded-citations. Attach literal evidence to cited primary pages using saved text and run its evidence verifier. A tracked failed source is not citable support. Retain official self-descriptions as attributed claims, not proof of their own truth. Neither first-edition reproduction nor original-language validation may be asserted unless performed.

## Parent verifier expectations

Verify hashes against this recorded acquisition metadata (do not reset expected pins to match changed files), offsets, exact quoted strings, context, unique expected case counts, source/evidence references, allowed labels, all seven note fields, and pending human status. Load only the inspected standalone quotation_verifier.py with `-B`, not application packages. Execute its verify_source_quote method with the recorded text pin, full quote, explicit span, and normalization=none. Store actual receipts under a new output directory, not inside historical source data. Source truth and semantic support remain not_assessed. Engineering should test tampering, malformed/missing IDs, false approval, and changed quote/context using synthetic fixtures, separately from historical evidence.
